1
00:00:05,541 --> 00:00:09,623
A flame flickers. Water
freezes. A person ages.

2
00:00:10,454 --> 00:00:15,198
This is how we picture change: a
noun, with verbs happening to it.

3
00:00:15,278 --> 00:00:18,119
There is a flame, and the flame flickers.

4
00:00:18,199 --> 00:00:20,266
The noun is the stable carrier.

5
00:00:20,346 --> 00:00:22,045
The verbs are what befall it.

6
00:00:22,125 --> 00:00:26,303
So when we ask what really changed,
we look for the carrier underneath.

7
00:00:27,087 --> 00:00:32,483
Look for it. The flame at this moment
is wax vapour, oxygen and light.

8
00:00:32,563 --> 00:00:35,961
They were not there a moment ago,
and they will be gone the next.

9
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:39,195
Nothing in the flame is the
flame across the minute.

10
00:00:39,275 --> 00:00:43,488
Take away the burning, and no flame
is left over to have been burning.

11
00:00:43,568 --> 00:00:46,400
The noun is never found
apart from the verbs.

12
00:00:47,217 --> 00:00:50,316
Yet the verbs are not found
apart from the noun either.

13
00:00:50,396 --> 00:00:55,112
A flickering with nothing flickering is no
more available than a flame that does not

14
00:00:55,192 --> 00:00:56,392
flicker.

15
00:00:56,893 --> 00:00:59,625
Nāgārjuna makes the point with walking.

16
00:00:59,705 --> 00:01:02,995
The walker and the walking
are designated together,

17
00:01:03,075 --> 00:01:05,563
named only in relation to each other.

18
00:01:05,643 --> 00:01:07,343
Neither is found first.

19
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:09,680
The same holds for changer and change.

20
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,663
Each needs the other to be named.

21
00:01:11,743 --> 00:01:14,371
Neither is a thing
waiting behind the naming.

22
00:01:15,198 --> 00:01:18,107
This is why the habit
is so hard to set down.

23
00:01:18,187 --> 00:01:20,336
It is not a belief about flames.

24
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:24,154
It is the grammar of a sentence,
subject then predicate,

25
00:01:24,234 --> 00:01:28,234
laid over experience and taken
for the shape of the world.

26
00:01:29,037 --> 00:01:33,318
The logic of dependency does not
replace the subject with a better one.

27
00:01:33,398 --> 00:01:36,769
Not a process, not a flow, not an energy.

28
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:40,506
It notices that changer and
change are designated together,

29
00:01:40,586 --> 00:01:43,305
within a frame of before and after.

30
00:01:43,385 --> 00:01:46,040
And that frame does not
stand on its own either.

31
00:01:46,849 --> 00:01:50,872
What remains is change, met
without a thing that changes.

32
00:01:50,952 --> 00:01:52,733
The candle still burns down.

33
00:01:52,813 --> 00:01:55,573
The wax is shorter at
midnight than at dusk.

34
00:01:55,653 --> 00:01:58,997
One can say correctly when it
was lit, and when it went out.

35
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,926
Nothing is lost from the burning.

36
00:02:01,006 --> 00:02:05,233
Only the passenger is let go: the
something that was meant to ride along

37
00:02:05,313 --> 00:02:09,504
underneath, staying the same while
everything about it differed.

38
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:12,514
The test is available at once.

39
00:02:12,594 --> 00:02:16,766
The next time a picture of something
changing arises, look for the something.

40
00:02:16,846 --> 00:02:19,869
Not in theory, but in
what is in front of you:

41
00:02:19,958 --> 00:02:23,302
the sound that is fading,
the thought that is passing,

42
00:02:23,382 --> 00:02:25,113
the flame that is leaning.

43
00:02:25,929 --> 00:02:28,906
Look for what is changing,
apart from the changing.

44
00:02:28,986 --> 00:02:31,256
The picture insists it must be there.

45
00:02:31,336 --> 00:02:34,721
The looking finds more
change, vivid and exact,

46
00:02:34,801 --> 00:02:36,492
and no changer behind it.

